---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseStudySection from "../../components/CaseStudySection.astro";

const threads = [
  {
    key: "infrastructure",
    label: "Infrastructure",
    owned: "Stepped into infrastructure ownership after scaling and downtime issues, and led the main site's move to serverless AWS ECS Fargate and RDS.",
    enables: "The team has a clearer hosting path for the website that Jisc's content and users depend on."
  },
  {
    key: "publishing",
    label: "Publishing",
    owned: "Maintained the Wagtail and Next.js publishing system with the Digital Experience Team.",
    enables: "Editors can keep the main site's content current while the application controls how it is presented."
  },
  {
    key: "delivery",
    label: "Delivery",
    owned: "Helped build Terraform-managed preview environments and added Playwright release validation.",
    enables: "The team can inspect a change and check key user paths before it reaches the main site."
  }
];
const mechanisms = [
  {
    thread: "infrastructure",
    layer: "Address the hosting failure mode",
    detail: "Scaling and downtime problems made infrastructure a product concern. The migration moved the main site to AWS ECS Fargate and RDS, with the publishing application still serving Jisc's public website."
  },
  {
    thread: "publishing",
    layer: "Keep editorial and application work connected",
    detail: "Wagtail manages content; Next.js presents it. Maintaining both sides matters when an editorial change needs to appear correctly on the public site."
  },
  {
    thread: "delivery",
    layer: "Inspect changes before release",
    detail: "Terraform-managed preview environments gave the team somewhere to review a change. Playwright validation checked user-facing behaviour as part of the release work."
  }
];
const initialThread = "infrastructure";
---

<CaseStudyLayout title="Jisc website" description="Infrastructure and publishing work on Jisc's main website, separate from Open Policy Finder." threads={threads} initialThread={initialThread}>
  <p slot="intro">Jisc's main site is a publishing product as well as a piece of infrastructure. I joined the Digital Experience Team's infrastructure work under a tight deadline after scaling and downtime issues, while maintaining the Wagtail and Next.js content system.</p>
  <dl slot="meta" class="case-meta" aria-label="Case study summary">
    <div><dt>Context</dt><dd>Jisc · Digital Experience Team / April 2024–February 2026</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>AWS ECS Fargate, RDS, Wagtail, Next.js, Terraform</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Project</dt><dd><a href="https://www.jisc.ac.uk">jisc.ac.uk</a></dd></div>
  </dl>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-problem" title="Problem">
    <p>Reliability issues on the main site had become urgent. At the same time, content editors still needed a usable publishing flow, and the team needed a way to review changes before release.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-contribution" title="My contribution">
    <table class="case-ledger">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">What I built and why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{threads.map((thread) => (
        <tr data-thread={thread.key} data-active={thread.key === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
          <th scope="row">{thread.label}</th><td><p>{thread.owned}</p><p>{thread.enables}</p></td>
        </tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-decisions" title="Decisions">
    <div class="case-prose">
      <table class="case-ledger">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Choice</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{mechanisms.map((mechanism) => (
          <tr data-thread={mechanism.thread} data-active={mechanism.thread === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
            <th scope="row">{mechanism.layer}</th><td>{mechanism.detail}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-result" title="What it enables">
    <div class="case-prose"><p>The main site moved to Fargate and RDS, and the team had a clearer path to preview and validate website changes. The migration, CMS work, and release checks belonged to the Digital Experience Team; my Open Policy Finder data and search work was a separate Jisc workstream.</p></div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-lesson" title="Lesson">
    <p>A public website's reliability, editorial workflow, and release path have to work together. Solving the urgent hosting problem also meant understanding how people changed and checked the site.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
